<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Identity-in-Christ on John, Complected</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/tags/identity-in-christ/</link><description>Recent content in Identity-in-Christ on John, Complected</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2026</copyright><lastBuildDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://john-nicholson.github.io/tags/identity-in-christ/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Remember Who You Are — Under His Wings</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-under-his-wings/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-under-his-wings/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke&amp;#43;1%3A5%E2%80%9325&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Luke 1:5–25&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;91&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 91&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There are seasons in life when we wait much longer than we expected. We pray, hope and trust, and sometimes wonder whether anything is changing at all. Some answers come quickly, while others seem to take years. In those long seasons, it can be easy to wonder whether God has forgotten us.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The story of Zechariah and Elizabeth reminds us that &lt;strong&gt;waiting is not the same as being forgotten&lt;/strong&gt;. They had lived faithfully for many years, prayed, served God and carried disappointment. By the time we meet them in Luke’s Gospel, they are both old, and the possibility of having a child seems to have passed.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Remember Who You Are — The Lord Is My Shepherd</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-the-lord-is-my-shepherd/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-the-lord-is-my-shepherd/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Joshua&amp;#43;14%3A6%E2%80%9314&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Joshua 14:6–14&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;23&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 23&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There is something powerful about looking back and seeing how faithfully God has led you.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There are seasons when the path has been clear and seasons when it has not. There are prayers that were answered quickly and others that took years. There are moments of joy, disappointment, waiting, change and unexpected blessing.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;And through all of it, &lt;strong&gt;God has been faithful&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Remember Who You Are — Nothing Can Separate You</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-nothing-can-separate-you/</link><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-nothing-can-separate-you/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis&amp;#43;5%3A21%E2%80%9324&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Genesis 5:21–24&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;, &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Hebrews&amp;#43;11%3A5%E2%80%936&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Hebrews 11:5–6&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt; and &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Romans&amp;#43;8%3A31%E2%80%9339&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Romans 8:31–39&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;73%3A23%E2%80%9328&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 73:23–28&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Fear often asks the same question in different ways: &lt;strong&gt;What if I am left on my own?&lt;/strong&gt; What if things change? What if I become weaker? What if I cannot remember what I used to remember, or cannot hold onto everything as tightly as I once did?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The Bible gives a very strong answer: &lt;strong&gt;you are not the one doing all the holding. God is holding you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Remember Who You Are — Remember Whose You Are</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-remember-whose-you-are/</link><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-remember-whose-you-are/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Romans&amp;#43;4%3A16%E2%80%9321&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Romans 4:16–21&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt; and &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Galatians&amp;#43;3%3A26%E2%80%9329&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Galatians 3:26–29&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;105%3A1%E2%80%9311&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 105:1–11&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There are moments when it helps to remember not only &lt;strong&gt;who we are&lt;/strong&gt;, but &lt;strong&gt;whose we are&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Life changes. Our strength changes. Our responsibilities change. Sometimes even the way we see ourselves can change. But if you belong to Jesus, there is something deeper than all of that.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You belong to God.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You are part of his family. You are part of a story that began long before you were born and will continue long after your own lifetime.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Remember Who You Are — I Have Called You by Name</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-i-have-called-you-by-name/</link><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-i-have-called-you-by-name/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis&amp;#43;12%3A1%E2%80%934&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Genesis 12:1–4&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt; and &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis&amp;#43;17%3A1%E2%80%937&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Genesis 17:1–7&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;139%3A1%E2%80%9318&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 139:1–18&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There can be something unsettling about feeling less certain of yourself than you once did. Names can become harder to remember. Familiar things can sometimes feel unfamiliar. Even our own story can become more difficult to hold together.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But God does not know us in the uncertain way that we sometimes know ourselves. &lt;strong&gt;He knows us completely.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Remember Who You Are — Greater Is He Who Is in You</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-greater-is-he-who-is-in-you/</link><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-greater-is-he-who-is-in-you/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1&amp;#43;John&amp;#43;4%3A4%E2%80%9318&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;1 John 4:4–18&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;56&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 56&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Fear can be very convincing. It can make a thought feel certain simply because it feels strong. It can make something small feel enormous, or make us feel that because we are frightened, the thing we fear must have power over us.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;John writes to believers with a very different perspective:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1&amp;#43;John&amp;#43;4%3A4&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;1 John 4:4&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That is not a promise that frightening things will never happen. It is a reminder about &lt;strong&gt;who is greater&lt;/strong&gt;. Fear is not greater. Confusion is not greater. The things we cannot explain are not greater. &lt;strong&gt;Jesus is greater.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Remember Who You Are — Do Not Be Afraid</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-do-not-be-afraid/</link><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-do-not-be-afraid/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Joshua&amp;#43;1%3A1%E2%80%939&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Joshua 1:1–9&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;27&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 27&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There are many things that can make us afraid. Sometimes we know exactly what we are frightened of; sometimes we simply feel afraid and cannot explain why. Our thoughts can become confused, things that once seemed familiar can feel uncertain, and we may wonder what is happening or what will happen next.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But there is something that has not changed: &lt;strong&gt;God is with you.&lt;/strong&gt; He has not moved away from you, he has not forgotten you, and he has not stopped loving you. Again and again in the Bible, God tells his people, &lt;strong&gt;“Do not be afraid.”&lt;/strong&gt; He does not say this because there is never anything frightening in life, but because we do not face those things alone.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>